.TH QFW-DEVICE-ACCESS.YAML 5 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw File Formats"
.SH NAME
qfw-device-access.yaml \- bind logical QFw devices to providers and credentials
.SH DESCRIPTION
The device-access configuration is a site-owned YAML file that maps logical
QFw device IDs to provider devices, API endpoints, and credential providers.
A service entry's
.B device-id
selects one device from this file.
.PP
The
.B service.device-access-config
field in
.BR qfw-site.yaml (5)
selects the active file. This separation allows a service manifest to describe
reusable QPM implementations while each site supplies its own devices,
endpoints, and credential integration.
.PP
Only the account running a device-backed QPM needs read access. The QPM manager
passes the selected path to the QPM process. Application processes do not
receive the file or provider credentials.
.SH QPUS MAPPING
The top-level
.B qpus
mapping contains one entry for each logical device ID.
.TP
.B provider
Provider implementation used by the device, such as
.BR iqm .
.TP
.B provider-device-id
Device name expected by the provider API. The logical QFw ID remains the key
under
.BR qpus .
.TP
.B url
Provider API endpoint.
.TP
.B credential-db
Path to a file-backed credential database. A relative path is resolved from
the directory containing the device-access file.
.TP
.B credential-provider
Name of an entry in the optional top-level
.B credential-providers
mapping. Use this instead of
.B credential-db
when a site integrates another credential source.
.TP
.B aliases
Optional alternate names that may resolve to this device.
.SH CREDENTIAL PROVIDERS
The optional
.B credential-providers
mapping defines named credential integrations. Supported provider types include
.BR file ,
.BR no-secret ,
and Python plugin providers. A file provider uses
.B credential-db
or
.BR path .
Its optional fields include
.BR refresh-policy ,
.BR ttl-ns ,
and
.BR ttl-seconds .
A plugin provider uses
.B module
and may select a class with
.BR class .
.SH SECURITY
The device-access file contains device endpoints and credential-provider
references. A referenced file credential database contains provider secrets
and must be readable only by the QPM service account. Keep both files outside
client-readable runtime directories.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
qpus:
  site-qpu:
    provider: iqm
    provider-device-id: default
    url: https://provider.example/
    credential-db: qpu-users.json
.EE
